---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Quick Revision | Engineering Interview Kit">
  <div class="space-y-8">
    <header class="mb-10 pb-8 border-b border-gray-800">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-amber-400 mb-4 tracking-tight flex items-center">
        <span class="mr-3">⚡</span> Quick Revision
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-400">Condensed 5-minute flash notes for last-minute interview prep.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert prose-blue max-w-none">
      <h2>Go</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Channels</strong>: Unbuffered (sync), Buffered (queue). Send to closed panics. Read from closed returns zero-value + false.</li>
        <li><strong>Goroutines</strong>: Lightweight threads. M:N scheduling. Multiplexed onto OS threads.</li>
        <li><strong>Mutex</strong>: Use `sync.Mutex` for exclusive locks, `sync.RWMutex` if many readers but few writers.</li>
        <li><strong>Defer</strong>: Executes in LIFO order (stack) right before the surrounding function returns.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>JavaScript</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Event Loop</strong>: Call Stack -> Microtasks (Promises) -> 1 Macrotask (setTimeout).</li>
        <li><strong>Closures</strong>: Function + its lexical environment. Retains access to outer scope after outer returns.</li>
        <li><strong>Hoisting</strong>: Declarations moved to top. `var` is `undefined`. `let/const` are in TDZ (Temporal Dead Zone).</li>
        <li><strong>this</strong>: Arrow functions inherit lexically. Regular functions depend on how they are called (`obj.func()`, `new`, `call`).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>TypeScript</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Interfaces vs Types</strong>: Interfaces can be merged (declaration merging). Types can use unions/intersections.</li>
        <li><strong>any vs unknown</strong>: `any` disables type checking. `unknown` forces you to narrow the type before using it.</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h2>SQL</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>ACID</strong>: Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability.</li>
        <li><strong>Indexes</strong>: B-Trees. Speed up reads, slow down writes. Covering index includes all columns needed by query.</li>
        <li><strong>Isolation Levels</strong>: Read Uncommitted, Read Committed, Repeatable Read, Serializable.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>System Design</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>CAP Theorem</strong>: Consistency, Availability, Partition Tolerance (Pick 2, usually CP or AP).</li>
        <li><strong>Caching</strong>: Cache-Aside, Write-Through, Write-Back. Use Redis/Memcached.</li>
        <li><strong>Load Balancing</strong>: Round Robin, Least Connections, IP Hash. Layer 4 (Transport) vs Layer 7 (App).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
